{"type":"message","id":"e024a4eb","parentId":"fa9d2b68","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:33:57.371Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it: `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\nNow let me:\n1. First read the README to understand the project and find \"Future Enhancements\"\n2. Spawn review-agent for code quality review\n3. Run dev server myself for functional testing","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到项目了：`/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n让我先读取 README 了解项目结构和 Future Enhancements 列表："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-6077defe94c74e9aad8cfb1a0d2952d6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/README.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-78da49825cb64b8bbd6aadab38660fda","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw-reports/leader-agent/2026-03-04-pixel-art-editor-complete.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":365,"output":191,"cacheRead":16575,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17131,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772595232731}}
{"type":"message","id":"ffdedb7d","parentId":"e024a4eb","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:33:57.379Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-6077defe94c74e9aad8cfb1a0d2952d6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs\n\nA real-time collaborative pixel art editor built with Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs). Based on [Jake Lazaroff's tutorial series](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/).\n\n## Features\n\n- 🎨 **Real-time Collaboration**: Multiple peers can draw simultaneously without conflicts\n- 🔄 **Offline Support**: Works offline and syncs automatically when back online\n- 📦 **98% Compression**: Binary encoding reduces sync data by up to 98%\n- 🖌️ **Smooth Drawing**: DDA line algorithm eliminates gaps when drawing fast\n- 🔌 **Network Simulation**: Toggle network and adjust latency to test sync behavior\n- 💾 **Conflict Resolution**: Last Write Wins (LWW) with peer ID tiebreaker\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n- **TypeScript** (strict mode)\n- **CRDT Data Structures**: LWWRegister, LWWMap\n- **Canvas 2D API** for rendering\n- **Pointer Events API** for drawing\n- **Binary Encoding** for compression\n- **No external dependencies** (Phase 1-3)\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Core CRDTs\n\n- **LWWRegister<T>**: Holds a single value with `[peerId, timestamp, value]` tuple\n- **LWWMap<T>**: Maps keys to LWWRegisters with tombstone deletions\n- **PixelData**: Thin wrapper over LWWMap for pixel coordinates\n\n### Editor\n\n- **PixelEditor**: Canvas-based editor with pointer event handling\n- DDA (Digital Differential Analyzer) line drawing algorithm\n- Timestamp optimization to reduce redundant updates\n\n### Encoding\n\n- **UUID Table**: Deduplicate peer IDs (63% reduction)\n- **Palette Table**: Deduplicate colors (71% reduction)\n- **Run-Length Encoding**: Compress blank pixels and runs (80% reduction)\n- **Binary Format**: Custom RIFF-like chunk format (94% reduction)\n- **Run-Length Binary**: Split data into separate chunks (98% reduction total)\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\nPixelArtEditor/\n├── src/\n│   ├── crdt/\n│   │   ├── LWWRegister.ts    # Last Write Wins Register\n│   │   ├── LWWMap.ts         # Last Write Wins Map\n│   │   └── PixelData.ts      # Pixel coordinate wrapper\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   └── PixelEditor.ts    # Canvas editor\n│   ├── encoding/\n│   │   ├── Encoder.ts        # State to binary\n│   │   └── Decoder.ts        # Binary to state\n│   └── types.ts              # TypeScript types\n├── tests/\n│   ├── LWWRegister.test.ts\n│   ├── LWWMap.test.ts\n│   ├── PixelData.test.ts\n│   └── encoding.test.ts\n├── index.html                # Demo page\n├── main.ts                   # Demo logic\n├── style.css\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n└── vite.config.ts\n```\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n```\n\n### Development\n\n```bash\n# Start dev server\nnpm run dev\n\n# The demo will open at http://localhost:3000\n```\n\n### Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run tests\nnpm test\n\n# Run tests in watch mode\nnpm run test:watch\n```\n\n### Building\n\n```bash\n# Build for production\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Basic Demo\n\nOpen `index.html` in a browser or run `npm run dev`. You'll see two canvases:\n\n1. **Draw** on either canvas by clicking and dragging\n2. **Change color** using the color picker\n3. **Toggle network** to simulate offline editing\n4. **Adjust latency** to see how CRDTs handle delayed sync\n\n### Programmatic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { PixelEditor } from \"./src/editor/PixelEditor.js\";\n\n// Create editor\nconst canvas = document.querySelector(\"canvas\");\nconst editor = new PixelEditor(canvas, { w: 100, h: 100 }, \"alice\");\n\n// Set color\neditor.color = [255, 0, 0];\n\n// Enable binary compression\neditor.compressionMode = \"binary\";\n\n// Handle state changes\neditor.onchange = (data) => {\n  // Send to peer (data is PixelDataState or Uint8Array)\n  sendToPeer(data);\n};\n\n// Receive peer updates\neditor.onmessage = (data) => {\n  editor.receive(data);\n};\n```\n\n## CRDT Fundamentals\n\n### Last Write Wins Register\n\nA register that stores a single value with metadata:\n```typescript\ntype LWWRegisterState<T> = [peerId: string, timestamp: number, value: T];\n```\n\n**Merge Algorithm**:\n1. If local timestamp > remote timestamp: keep local\n2. If timestamps equal and local peer ID > remote peer ID: keep local\n3. Otherwise: overwrite with remote\n\n### Last Write Wins Map\n\nA map where each key has its own LWWRegister:\n```typescript\ntype LWWMapState<T> = Record<string, LWWRegisterState<T | null>>;\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Deletions use tombstones (set to `null`)\n- Each key merges independently\n- Composition enables complex structures\n\n### Binary Format\n\n```\n[INFO chunk]     - Magic \"CRDT\" + artboard width\n[UUID chunk]     - Deduplicated peer IDs (16 bytes each)\n[PLTT chunk]     - Color palette (3 bytes each, index 0 reserved for erased)\n[TIME chunk]     - Timestamps (run-length encoded)\n[WRTR chunk]     - Writer IDs (run-length encoded)\n[COLR chunk]     - Color indices (run-length encoded)\n```\n\n## Performance\n\n| Format        | Size (100x100) | Reduction |\n|---------------|----------------|-----------|\n| JSON          | ~648 KB        | -         |\n| Hex Codes     | ~606 KB        | 6%        |\n| UUID Table    | ~236 KB        | 63%       |\n| Palette Table | ~187 KB        | 71%       |\n| RLE           | ~129 KB        | 80%       |\n| Binary        | ~40 KB         | 94%       |\n| Run-Length Binary | ~14 KB    | 98%       |\n\n## Testing\n\nThe project includes comprehensive unit tests for:\n\n- ✅ LWWRegister merge behavior\n- ✅ LWWMap CRUD operations and merge\n- ✅ PixelData coordinate handling\n- ✅ Binary encoding/decoding roundtrip\n- ✅ Run-length encoding\n- ✅ Error handling\n\n## Development Phases\n\n1. ✅ **Phase 1: Core CRDTs** - LWWRegister, LWWMap, PixelData\n2. ✅ **Phase 2: Pixel Editor UI** - Canvas, pointer events, DDA\n3. ✅ **Phase 3: State Synchronization** - Network simulation\n4. ✅ **Phase 4: Binary Encoding** - 98% compression\n5. ✅ **Phase 5: Testing & Polish** - Tests, benchmarks, docs\n\n## References\n\n- [An Interactive Intro to CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/)\n- [Building a Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/building-a-collaborative-pixel-art-editor-with-crdts/)\n- [Making CRDTs 98% More Efficient](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/making-crdts-98-percent-more-efficient/)\n\n## License\n\nMIT"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772595237377}}
{"type":"message","id":"a7af8a3a","parentId":"ffdedb7d","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:33:57.386Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-78da49825cb64b8bbd6aadab38660fda","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Pixel Art Editor - Phase 1-5 Completion Report\n\n**Project:** Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs\n**Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Status:** ✅ COMPLETE\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nSuccessfully implemented a collaborative pixel art editor using Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs) with 98% binary compression. All 5 development phases completed with 42 passing unit tests.\n\n---\n\n## Completed Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Core CRDTs ✅\n\n**Implemented:**\n- `LWWRegister<T>` - Last Write Wins Register with peer ID tiebreaker\n- `LWWMap<T>` - Last Write Wins Map with tombstone deletions\n- `PixelData` - Coordinate wrapper over LWWMap for RGB colors\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Timestamp-based conflict resolution\n- Peer ID tiebreaker for concurrent writes\n- Monotonic state growth (no deletions, only tombstones)\n- Full TypeScript generics support\n\n**Files:**\n- `src/crdt/LWWRegister.ts` (1761 bytes)\n- `src/crdt/LWWMap.ts` (2786 bytes)\n- `src/crdt/PixelData.ts` (2059 bytes)\n\n**Tests:** 14/14 passing\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Pixel Editor UI ✅\n\n**Implemented:**\n- `PixelEditor` class with Canvas 2D rendering\n- Pointer event handling (down/move/up)\n- DDA line drawing algorithm\n- Timestamp optimization (prevents redundant pixel updates)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Smooth drawing without gaps\n- High-DPI display support\n- Crosshair cursor\n- Touch-action disabled for touch devices\n\n**Files:**\n- `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts` (7450 bytes)\n\n**Tests:** Integrated in main workflow\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: State Synchronization ✅\n\n**Implemented:**\n- Network simulation (toggle on/off)\n- Adjustable latency slider (0-2000ms)\n- State exchange mechanism\n- Automatic merge on state change\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Offline support with automatic sync\n- Latency simulation for testing\n- Visual online/offline indicators\n- Event-driven state propagation\n\n**Files:**\n- `index.html` (1539 bytes)\n- `main.ts` (2783 bytes)\n- `style.css` (1630 bytes)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Binary Encoding ✅\n\n**Implemented:**\n- `Encoder` class - state to binary conversion\n- `Decoder` class - binary to state conversion\n- 6-stage compression pipeline\n- RIFF-like chunk format\n\n**Compression Pipeline:**\n1. Hex codes (6% reduction)\n2. UUID table deduplication (63% reduction)\n3. Palette table deduplication (71% reduction)\n4. Run-length encoding for blanks (80% reduction)\n5. Binary format (94% reduction)\n6. **Total: 98% reduction** (648 KB → 14 KB)\n\n**Binary Format:**\n```\n[INFO] - Magic \"CRDT\" + width + height\n[UUID] - Deduplicated peer IDs (16 bytes each)\n[PLTT] - Color palette (3 bytes each, index 0 reserved for erased)\n[DATA] - Pixel data with run-length encoding (blank runs + pixels)\n```\n\n**Files:**\n- `src/encoding/Encoder.ts` (7163 bytes)\n- `src/encoding/Decoder.ts` (4102 bytes)\n\n**Tests:** 12/12 passing\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: Testing & Polish ✅\n\n**Implemented:**\n- Comprehensive unit test suite (42 tests)\n- TypeScript strict mode configuration\n- Jest testing framework with ESM support\n- Production-ready documentation\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- LWWRegister: merge behavior, generic types, edge cases\n- LWWMap: CRUD operations, merge, tombstones, conflict resolution\n- PixelData: coordinate handling, default values, convergent merges\n- Encoding: roundtrip, compression ratio, error handling\n\n**Files:**\n- `tests/LWWRegister.test.ts` (1789 bytes)\n- `tests/LWWMap.test.ts` (3254 bytes)\n- `tests/PixelData.test.ts` (3537 bytes)\n- `tests/encoding.test.ts` (4650 bytes)\n- `README.md` (6171 bytes)\n\n**Test Results:** 42/42 passing ✅\n\n---\n\n## Project Statistics\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Total Files | 20 |\n| Source Files | 11 |\n| Test Files | 4 |\n| Lines of Code | ~3,000 |\n| Test Coverage | 100% (core modules) |\n| TypeScript Strict Mode | ✅ |\n| External Dependencies | 0 (core), dev only |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     PixelEditor                          │\n│  ┌──────────────┐         ┌──────────────┐             │\n│  │   Canvas UI  │  ↔      │  PixelData   │             │\n│  │  (Drawing)   │         │   (CRDT)     │             │\n│  └──────────────┘         └──────┬───────┘             │\n│                                  │                      │\n│                                  ▼                      │\n│                          ┌──────────────┐              │\n│                          │   LWWMap    │              │\n│                          └──────┬───────┘              │\n│                                 │                      │\n│                ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐     │\n│                ▼                                 ▼     │\n│         ┌──────────────┐                 ┌──────────────┐\n│         │ LWWRegister  │                 │ LWWRegister  │\n│         │   (per key)  │   ...           │   (per key)  │\n│         └──────────────┘                 └──────────────┘\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nBinary Encoding Pipeline:\nState → [UUID Dedup] → [Palette Dedup] → [RLE] → [Binary] → 98% compressed\n```\n\n---\n\n## Compression Benchmarks\n\n| Format | Size (100x100) | Reduction |\n|--------|----------------|-----------|\n| JSON (uncompressed) | 648 KB | - |\n| Hex Codes | 606 KB | 6% |\n| UUID Table | 236 KB | 63% |\n| Palette Table | 187 KB | 71% |\n| Run-Length Encoding | 129 KB | 80% |\n| Binary Format | 40 KB | 94% |\n| **Run-Length Binary** | **14 KB** | **98%** |\n\n---\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Demo\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n# Opens http://localhost:3000 with two collaborative canvases\n```\n\n### Programmatic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { PixelEditor } from \"./src/editor/PixelEditor.js\";\n\nconst canvas = document.querySelector(\"canvas\");\nconst editor = new PixelEditor(canvas, { w: 100, h: 100 }, \"alice\");\n\n// Enable 98% compression\neditor.compressionMode = \"binary\";\n\n// Handle changes\neditor.onchange = (data) => sendToPeer(data);\n\n// Receive updates\nonPeerMessage = (data) => editor.receive(data);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Technical Highlights\n\n### CRDT Merge Algorithm (LWWRegister)\n```typescript\nmerge(state: [peerId: string, timestamp: number, value: T]): void {\n  if (localTimestamp > remoteTimestamp) return; // Keep local\n  if (timestampsEqual && localPeerId > remotePeerId) return; // Keep local\n  this.state = state; // Accept remote\n}\n```\n\n### DDA Line Drawing\n```typescript\n// Draws smooth lines between cursor positions without gaps\nconst steps = Math.max(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));\nconst xInc = dx / steps;\nconst yInc = dy / steps;\n```\n\n### Run-Length Binary Encoding\n```typescript\n// Blank pixels: [TAG_BLANK, countHi, countLo]\n// Colored pixels: [TAG_PIXEL, writerId, timestamp, colorId]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **Network Simulation Only**: No real WebSocket implementation (demo uses local sync)\n2. **Canvas Size Fixed**: 100x100 artboard (configurable but requires re-init)\n3. **No Undo/Redo**: Not implemented in current version\n4. **Single Color**: No brush size or opacity options\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n- [ ] Real WebSocket/RTC network layer\n- [ ] Undo/Redo with CRDT history\n- [ ] Brush size and opacity\n- [ ] Export to PNG/SVG\n- [ ] Layer support\n- [ ] Fill tool\n- [ ] Eraser tool\n- [ ] Zoom/Pan functionality\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [An Interactive Intro to CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/)\n- [Building a Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/building-a-collaborative-pixel-art-editor-with-crdts/)\n- [Making CRDTs 98% More Efficient](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/making-crdts-98-percent-more-efficient/)\n\n---\n\n## Deliverables Checklist\n\n- ✅ LWWRegister implementation\n- ✅ LWWMap implementation\n- ✅ PixelData implementation\n- ✅ PixelEditor with Canvas rendering\n- ✅ Pointer event handling\n- ✅ DDA line drawing\n- ✅ Network simulation\n- ✅ Binary encoder (98% compression)\n- ✅ Binary decoder\n- ✅ Unit test suite (42 tests, all passing)\n- ✅ Demo HTML page\n- ✅ Documentation (README.md)\n- ✅ TypeScript strict mode\n- ✅ Package configuration\n\n---\n\n**Project Completion Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Total Development Time:** ~2 hours\n**Lines of Code:** ~3,000\n**Test Pass Rate:** 100% (42/42)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772595237385}}
